<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Justin Ahomadégbé-Tomêtin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1917–2002</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Justin Ahomadégbé</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Justin Ahomadégbé-Tomêtin was a Dahomeyan politician, a dentist from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abomey">Abomey</a> whose support lay in the Fon south-centre. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hubert-maga">Hubert Maga</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sourou-migan-apithy">Sourou Migan Apithy</a> he formed the regional rivalry that dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-dahomey">Dahomey</a>'s politics after 1946 and through the coups of the 1960s. He was head of government in 1964–1965 and chaired the rotating Presidential Council in 1972 until the coup of Mathieu Kérékou.</p></div>
